  "notes": "From the model table: **16 GPON service ports** and **4x 10GE/GE upstream ports**, 140 Gbit/s switching capacity, 1024 ONTs. The upstream ports are 10GE/GE cages, so `speedCaps` carries both 1000 and 10000 rather than a bare 10G - a GE optic in the cage must run at 1G. The GPON service ports are 2.5G downstream / 1.25G upstream, which is what `speedCaps: [1244, 2488]` records on every OLT in this catalogue. The datasheet publishes **no ferrule polish** for the PON connectors; `sc-apc` is this catalogue's PON default and matches every other OLT here, so it is an inherited convention rather than a quoted fact - recorded because a UPC/APC mismatch is a real, invisible loss. The sixteen-PON member, and the only one that scales past 256 ONTs (1024), which is the reason to pick it over the GP08-H3."
